# Who may read and write what on the broker (mosquitto.conf's acl_file). Anything not granted here is refused, so a
# device's password, if it leaks, can't speak for another device: above all, only the lock may say the door was opened
# (TARS puts whoever opens it from outside at home, docs/presence.md#the-front-door).
#
# Mosquitto reads this again on a SIGHUP (deploy/install-pi.sh sends one), or docker restart mosquitto.

# Home Assistant works every device, the lock included, so it reads and writes everything.
user homeassistant
topic readwrite #

# TARS only listens to what the locks did; it writes nothing.
user tars
topic read nuki/+/lockActionEvent

# Every other user is a device: its own topics, under its user's name (the Nuki lock's user is nuki, and its topics
# are nuki/<its id>/...; Zigbee2MQTT's are zigbee2mqtt/...), and Home Assistant's discovery, where it announces
# itself. A device whose topics are under another name needs its own lines above, as Home Assistant's are.
pattern readwrite %u/#
pattern readwrite homeassistant/#
